# imperial_codex — Continue.dev Project Rules
# These rules are injected into every chat and agent session automatically.

## Stack
- Next.js 16.2 / App Router, React 19, TypeScript 5, Node.js 20 LTS
- Package manager: npm only (never yarn or pnpm)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL via @supabase/supabase-js)
  - All write operations use exponential back-off: base 500 ms, cap 5000 ms, max 2 retries
- Caching: Redis
- Vector search: Qdrant (primary), Pinecone (secondary)
- AI (primary): OpenAI GPT-4o via Vercel AI SDK — streamText / generateText
- AI (secondary): Anthropic Claude 3.5 Sonnet — always include a fallback strategy
- Embeddings: OpenAI text-embedding-3-large (1536 dims)
- Auth: iron-session (cookie-based), clearance levels 0–2
- Encryption: AES-256-GCM for vault data

## Naming Conventions
- Directories and non-component files: kebab-case
- React components: PascalCase (e.g., ChatWidget.tsx)
- JSON data files: SNAKE_UPPER_CASE (e.g., CAPITAL_ALLOCATIONS.json)
- All source code lives under src/

## Code Quality
- Use exact / pinned versions in package.json — no open ranges
- Never interpolate user input into SQL — always use parameterized queries
- Validate and sanitise all external inputs
- Prefer async/await over raw Promise chains
- Export types from the module where they are defined

## Testing
- Write Jest tests for every new function or module
- Use fast-check for property-based tests on pure functions
- Run tests with: npm test (not watch mode)
- Type-check with: npm run typecheck before marking a task done
- Lint with: npm run lint before committing

## Git
- Commit messages follow Conventional Commits:
    <type>(<scope>): <short summary>
    Types: feat | fix | docs | style | refactor | test | chore
- Never push directly to main — always use a feature branch
- Never commit: .env, .p12, .pem, .key, auth.json, or any secrets

## Security
- Secrets must only be read from environment variables, never hard-coded
- Use AWS Secrets Manager or Vercel encrypted env vars for production secrets
- Sanitise all user-provided content before rendering (XSS prevention)
- All API routes must validate the session and clearance level before operating
